ralph/prd.json:4675:      "notes": "Authorization coverage for GET /v1/services/{service_id}/rendered. Implemented internal/controlplane/httpapi/services_rendered_policy_test.go porting the BE-0186 services_get policy matrix to the /rendered route with distinct canonical fixtures (canonicalRenderedSvcForMatrix, renderedSvcDenyBodyLeak) and an allow-path assertion helper (assertRenderedAllowPath) that pins the rendered envelope schema, service projection, Dokploy-safe name, type, and the deterministic 4-label structural attribution. Reuses the existing serviceIDResolver fixtures (getServiceHandlerForIdentity) and rendered wire shapes (decodeRenderedServiceBody) from BE-0186 / BE-0196 — no production change. Verified gofmt, go vet ./..., go test ./..., go test -race ./..."
ralph/prd.json:4689:        "Secrets, tokens, API keys, cookies, and rendered environment variable values are redacted in logs, errors, audit metadata, and test output."
ralph/prd.json:4694:      "notes": "Endpoint belongs to the variables backend surface. Implemented GET /v1/services/{service_id}/variables: migration 0021_service_variables (composite FK to services(organization_id, id), per-service key uniqueness, optimistic-concurrency version trigger), domain.KindServiceVariable='svar', store.ServiceVariableRepository.ListByService + store.ServiceVariableReader.ListServiceVariables (Gets service first inside Store.Read tx so cross-tenant or unknown service_id surfaces as apierr.NotFound), httpapi.listServiceVariablesHandler with redaction chokepoint (secret values render as output.Sentinel, non-secret verbatim), route registered with action env.read on serviceIDResolver, contract+OpenAPI tests, integration tests with two-tenant isolation + sibling service isolation. NewHandler/newRouteTable signatures grew one positional port (serviceVariables ServiceVariableReader) at the tail of the service-ports group; sweep across 53 test files. gofmt/go vet/go test/go test -race all green."
ralph/prd.json:4708:        "Secrets, tokens, API keys, cookies, and rendered environment variable values are redacted in logs, errors, audit metadata, and test output."
ralph/prd.json:4727:        "Secrets, tokens, API keys, cookies, and rendered environment variable values are redacted in logs, errors, audit metadata, and test output."
ralph/prd.json:4732:      "notes": "Authorization coverage for GET /v1/services/{service_id}/variables. Implemented internal/controlplane/httpapi/service_variables_policy_test.go porting the BE-0198 services_rendered policy matrix to the env.read action on serviceIDResolver (action env.read on the same bare-id resource shape: principal-home org + path service_id, no ProjectID leg). Adds a per-matrix canonical fixture (canonicalSvcVarsServiceID / canonicalServiceVariables / canonicalSvcVarsSecretPlaintext) plus svcVarsDenyBodyLeak — the secret-plaintext-anchored deny-path leak guard layered on top of the structural leak guard, mirroring environment_variables_policy_test.go (BE-0174) for the env-id route — and an allow-path assertion helper (assertSvcVarsAllowPath) that pins the listServiceVariables envelope schema, redaction chokepoint (secret values render as output.Sentinel), and the non-secret-verbatim contract. Reuses existing service-variables wire fixtures (listServiceVariablesHandlerFor, getServiceVariables, decodeListServiceVariables, fakeServiceVariableReader, seedServiceVariableWire) from service_variables_test.go and the shared orgPrincipal / decodeError helpers — no production change. Verified gofmt, go vet ./..., go test ./..., go test -race ./..."
