ralph/prd.json:6746:      "notes": "Pinned the compose renderer contract in internal/controlplane/dokploy/renderer_compose_test.go: ServiceCompose preserved across dockerfile and nixpacks builders, SubtypeBoundaryFromApplication asserts compose stays compose and application stays application (with yalla.service-type label carrying the rendered type), RoleMatrix across (builder × role) with Image/ArtifactURL/Engine stay empty invariants, ValidationFailures table including image-builder-missing-image, drop-artifact-builder-missing-artifact-url, and bad-builder, TierResourceDefaults pinning the load-bearing production-web → 2 replica default for compose (the same as application), RedactsAllVariableValuesAcrossRoles, and per-builder determinism. Worker / dokploy_refs / quota-conversion seam defers to a later worker story; renderer-side determinism + service-type-preservation invariants are the structural barrier the worker depends on. gofmt, go vet ./..., go test ./..., and go test -race ./... pass."
ralph/prd.json:6760:        "Secrets, tokens, API keys, cookies, and rendered environment variable values are redacted in logs, errors, audit metadata, and test output."
ralph/prd.json:6779:        "Secrets, tokens, API keys, cookies, and rendered environment variable values are redacted in logs, errors, audit metadata, and test output."
ralph/prd.json:6784:      "notes": "Service type: postgres. Renderer-side contract pinned at internal/controlplane/dokploy/renderer_database_postgres_test.go: subtype identity (Type=ServiceDatabase + Engine=EnginePostgres), application/compose subtype boundary (yalla.engine label distinguishes engines, yalla.service-type stays database), drops role+domains+cron-schedule, validation including missing-engine and unsupported-engine (sqlite) cases with no value echo, tier resource defaults (database services do not participate in the production-web 2-replica bump), secrets redaction across Summary JSON / slog record / Summary.String, and byte-stable determinism. Production code is additive: EnginePostgres constant, validEngine() whitelist gate in Render(), and a new yalla.engine label emitted by renderLabels() for ServiceDatabase services (database.golden refreshed accordingly). Worker-side dokploy_refs atomic write, fake Dokploy create/update/deploy/poll/failure/retry/replay, and quota reservation-to-conversion flow defer to the later database worker story per the BE-0301 deferral pattern. The validEngine whitelist is the production-code seam BE-0311 mysql / BE-0313 mariadb / BE-0315 mongo / BE-0317 redis each extend by one constant."
