ralph/progress.txt:30047:- Added internal/controlplane/httpapi/environments_delete_contract_test.go closing the three contract-test criteria not directly asserted by environments_delete_test.go (BE-0160) or environments_delete_policy_test.go (BE-0162). Structural twin of environments_update_contract_test.go (BE-0158) and environments_get_contract_test.go (BE-0155), adapted to the DELETE single-environment shape: no JSON body, 202 Accepted success, EnvironmentDeleter port, action environment.delete, scheduled-deletion semantics rendered with a deletion_scheduled_at stamp and a version-pinned ETag header.
ralph/progress.txt:30050:  - TestDeleteEnvironmentRequestLogRedactsBearerToken: pinned both legs (success with RoleOwner, deny with Disabled=true) using a recognisable bearer credential `yk_live_supersecret_environments_delete_DEADBEEF0123456789`; asserts the credential is absent from both the structured log JSON and the response body. The deny-leg deleter errors if invoked, proving the leak axis is not "deleter rendered the bearer into an error string".
ralph/progress.txt:30068:  - The DELETE wire shape has no secret-bearing fields (display_name, slug, version, deletion_scheduled_at are all public), so the "marker absence in response body" assertion only needs to scan for the bearer credential — there is no need for an additional per-row marker over a secret-bearing field. Contrast: a future contract test for an endpoint that returns rendered environment variables (BE-0173 / BE-0176) would also need to seed a `RENDERED_VAR_MARKER` into the variable value and assert its absence from the response body for non-superuser principals.
ralph/progress.txt:31522:- Tests prove: (a) Upsert INSERT branch returns the committed row with version=1, byte-equal CreatedAt/UpdatedAt (no UPDATE trigger has fired yet), all caller-supplied fields echoed verbatim, nil ServiceID stays nil; (b) Upsert INSERT with non-nil service_id round-trips the pointer to the exact text and accepts principal_kind="sa" alongside "usr"; (c) Upsert UPDATE branch on the scope-tuple conflict mutates ONLY role, bumps version via the environment_grants_bump_version trigger, refreshes updated_at via the environment_grants_set_updated_at trigger, preserves created_at, IGNORES the caller-supplied id (persisted id stays at baseline's id), preserves principal_kind (cross-kind smuggling impossible — the caller's "sa" does not stick when baseline is "usr"), and preserves the immutable identifiers (organization_id, environment_id, principal_id, service_id); (d) Upsert with cross-tenant environment_id surfaces typed apierr.Conflict via the MATCH SIMPLE composite FK (organization_id, environment_id) -> environments; (e) Upsert with unknown environment_id under the caller's tenant lands on the same typed Conflict for the same FK reason; (f) Upsert with duplicate primary key (different principal_id so the scope-tuple ON CONFLICT branch does NOT match) surfaces typed Conflict via the PRIMARY KEY (id) constraint; (g) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs with nil keepIDs clears all grants of (org, env); (h) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs with empty-slice keepIDs is identical to nil; (i) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs with a non-empty keepIDs keeps exactly the listed ids and drops every other row; (j) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs is tenant-scoped — a cross-tenant environmentID under the caller's organization_id matches zero rows, leaving the other tenant's bystander grant byte-untouched and the caller's own grant intact; (k) ON DELETE CASCADE from environments removes every environment_grants row when the parent environments row is deleted directly (NOT via ScheduleDeletion which is a soft delete); (l) Upsert rolls back when the surrounding Write closure returns a non-nil error — the row does not surface at ListByEnvironment outside the rolled-back transaction (the only observation surface for grants); (m) nil-Tx guards on Upsert AND DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs render typed apierr.Internal — never a nil-pointer panic.
ralph/progress.txt:31574:- Tests prove: (a) Insert returns the committed row with version=1, byte-equal CreatedAt/UpdatedAt (no UPDATE trigger has fired yet), nil DeletionScheduledAt, and round-trips identity (id/org/project/env/slug/name/kind) plus GetByID re-read agrees; (b) Update bumps version by exactly +1 via services_bump_version, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves Kind (the SET clause must touch slug/display_name only — Kind is immutable Dokploy taxonomy enforced by the migration-0002 CHECK), preserves the composite (organization_id, project_id, environment_id) tenant key (Update is a PATCH, not a re-parenting), and leaves DeletionScheduledAt nil on a live row; (c) Update with matching If-Match succeeds (positive companion to the stale-If-Match conflict path through classifyServiceConcurrencyMiss); (d) ScheduleDeletion bumps version, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves identity (slug/display_name/kind), preserves the composite tenant key, and stamps deletion_scheduled_at at or after baseline.UpdatedAt; (e) Restore is the inverse projected through the same dual-anchor — bumps version, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves identity and the composite tenant key, and clears deletion_scheduled_at back to NULL (the load-bearing assertion since a missing `SET deletion_scheduled_at = NULL` would still trip the version/updated_at anchors); (f) Insert participates in the surrounding transaction as the unit of work — a closure error rolls the row back so GetByID surfaces NotFound AND ListByEnvironment does not see it; (g/h/i) nil-Tx guards on Insert, Update, and ScheduleDeletion render typed apierr.Internal — never a nil-pointer panic (Restore's nil-Tx guard is already covered by TestServiceRepositoryRestoreRejectsNilTx in service_restore_test.go).
ralph/progress.txt:31648:  - The "leaf-table grant" shape (service_grants) is a structural simplification of the BE-0441 environment_grants template: the schema HAS no nullable scope pointer (no service_id pointer because the service IS the leaf), so the unique index needs NO COALESCE, the row-shape needs no *string pointer, the Upsert signature drops the trailing pointer arg, the renderer-side scope dedup key needs no \x00 separator, and the ListByService ORDER BY is two-column (principal_id ASC, id ASC) instead of three-column. EVERY test in the env-grant invariants template that exercised the nullable-pointer path (round-trip pointer, NULLS-FIRST ordering, dedup-with-empty-string COALESCE) collapses to a one-leg test or drops out entirely — the BE-0447 file is ~85% of the BE-0443 file size as a result.
ralph/progress.txt:31967:- Implemented: internal/controlplane/store/quota_policy_tenant_isolation_test.go — repository-layer tenant-isolation tests for the quota_policies table. quota_policies is a dual-scope table (plan_default OR organization) whose ONLY mutation surface is UpsertOrganizationPolicy and whose row body is only observable through the typed resolvers (EffectiveLimit / ListEffectiveLimits / ListOrganizationUsage). No per-id Get / Update / Delete surface exists, so the cross-tenant guarantee at this layer is exhaustively the projection invariant on every resolver leg AND the byte-identical-bystander invariant on the upsert. Coverage (9 tests): (1) EffectiveLimit per-resource is tenant-scoped — orgB's override does not appear when orgA queries the same resource; (2) ListEffectiveLimits rendered count is local to the queried tenant (orgA=1, orgB=3) — no count cross; (3) shared-resource isolation (both tenants override `projects` with distinct limit/mode — each sees its OWN); (4) plan isolation (orgA on 'starter' must not see 'pro' plan defaults); (5) ListOrganizationUsage is tenant scoped at BOTH the policies CTE and the usage CTE; (6) shared-counter isolation (both tenants have a quota_usage counter for the same resource with distinct used_value); (7) Upsert INSERT branch on orgA leaves orgB's bystander row byte-identical (the SAME resource on both tenants — the ON CONFLICT predicate is exercised); (8) Upsert UPDATE branch on orgA leaves orgB's bystander row byte-identical (both tenants pre-seeded with an override on the SAME resource — the maximally adversarial fixture for the partial-unique-index ON CONFLICT target); (9) same-resource upserts in two tenants both succeed (positive-direction pair for the bystander proofs — proves the partial unique index is per-tenant, not global).
ralph/progress.txt:32236:  - The deployments table stores NO secret-bearing column (source_ref is a branch/commit/tag/image name; error_message is redacted by the worker before persistence). The BE-0434-style raw-secret probe and the redaction-needle-in-error probe have no analogue here — but the BE-0458 acceptance criteria still apply structurally: rendered environment variable values, tokens, API keys and cookies do not appear on this table because they live in their own scoped tables.
ralph/progress.txt:32476:  - **Bare-id services route inherits the no-secret-on-wire property from environmentService** (BE-0185): GET /v1/services/{service_id} renders the canonical row through environmentServiceOf, whose wire shape is id, organization_id, project_id, environment_id, slug, display_name, kind, version, created_at, updated_at, and an optional deletion_scheduled_at. None of those are bearer- or secret-bearing, so the redaction tests only need to prove the BEARER doesn't leak; there is no "submitted-secret redaction" leg (cf. BE-0176 for endpoints whose body carries secret values). This property is shared with environments_get / projects_get / project_environments_get / api_keys_get's wire shapes.
