diff --git a/ralph/progress.txt b/ralph/progress.txt
index 08d8dfb390eb91a474ce8dde1c21d545625aefe5..fe05b4ae89a649f09aece1926bb5147218ea9b90
--- a/ralph/progress.txt
+++ b/ralph/progress.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Repository CRUD-and-invariants tests for a **tenant-scoped service leaf table whose public surface is Insert + GetByID + ListByService + Update + DeleteByID, whose row has database-owned version/created_at/updated_at, and whose parent link is the composite `(organization_id, service_id)` FK** (BE-0475 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/service_domain_repository_invariants_test.go for service_domains). The reusable shape is: seed the Organization -> Project -> Environment -> Service chain with existing helpers, insert through the typed repository rather than raw SQL, assert version=1 and created_at==updated_at on INSERT, assert Update bumps version and advances updated_at while preserving created_at and identity fields, assert matching If-Match succeeds while stale If-Match on Update/Delete returns typed `E_CONFLICT`, assert DeleteByID returns the final row and removes it, and cover CHECK/FK/UNIQUE violations, transaction rollback, parent cascade, deterministic ListByService ordering, and nil-Tx guards. Forward-applicable to future service-scoped leaf tables with hard-delete lifecycle and optimistic concurrency.
 - Repository CRUD-and-invariants tests for a **TABLE WHOSE *_repository.go + PRIMARY *_test.go + INTERNAL *_internal_test.go + CANONICAL *_canonical_test.go ALL ALREADY EXIST FROM A PRIOR (NON-PRD) SUBSYSTEM STORY + VALIDATOR-EXHAUSTIVENESS STORY, AND WHOSE LIFECYCLE IS APPEND + READ + ONE STATE-TRANSITION (MarkRevoked, *Tx-bound) WITH A REPOSITORY-LEVEL LIMIT CAP, AND WHOSE UPDATE SURFACE IS GUARDED BY THREE STACKED BEFORE-UPDATE TRIGGERS (set_updated_at + bump_version + a per-column rewrite-rejecting trigger), AND WHOSE Append FILLS A ZERO StartedAt SERVER-SIDE IN THE REPOSITORY (not via DB DEFAULT)** (BE-0473 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/break_glass_repository_invariants_test.go for break_glass_sessions). Subspecies of the BE-0469 (idempotency_keys) gap-fill pattern with five load-bearing deltas: (a) the THREE-trigger UPDATE surface is unique in store — the rewrite-rejecting trigger (break_glass_sessions_reject_rewrite) raises SQLSTATE 23001 (restrict_violation) for any UPDATE that mutates a non-revocation column AND for any UPDATE that blanks the reason column. The test file walks the FULL trigger predicate matrix (id, organization_id, actor_id, actor_kind, reason, started_at, expires_at, request_id, correlation_id) via raw-SQL UPDATEs and asserts BOTH the typed error AND byte-identical row re-load AFTER the rejection. A regression that demoted any single column from the trigger predicate would surface as a per-case failure on its first iteration. The existing primary _test.go's TestBreakGlassSchemaRejectsUpdateToImmutableColumns covers ONLY reason rewrite, so the per-column-matrix invariants probe is genuinely new coverage. (b) The Append fills a zero StartedAt server-side via `if s.StartedAt.IsZero() { s.StartedAt = time.Now().UTC() }` BEFORE the INSERT — the column has NO DEFAULT in the migration (vs created_at/updated_at which DO have DEFAULT now()). A regression that removed the IsZero branch would NOT surface as a CHECK violation (expires_at > started_at is satisfied with zero started_at + any future expires_at) — it would silently store year-0001 rows. TestBreakGlassRepositoryAppendStartedAtDefaultsToNow is the regression backstop: it asserts the filled StartedAt falls within a ±2s wallclock bracket. (c) MarkRevoked's UPDATE filters on `revoked_at IS NULL` (column predicate, NOT row-existence predicate) — same shape as DriftFindingRepository.MarkResolved (BE-0471). The zero-rows branch falls through to a tenant-scoped follow-up Get inside the SAME *Tx to distinguish "missing" (typed apierr.NotFound, caller-supplied id) from "already revoked" (typed apierr.Conflict). This means TestBreakGlassRepositoryMarkRevokedCrossTenantIsNotFound is NOT redundant with TestBreakGlassRepositoryGetCrossTenantIsNotFound: a regression that dropped tenant scoping from BOTH the UPDATE and the follow-up Get would silently succeed in revoking another tenant's session. The cross-tenant Get + cross-tenant MarkRevoked pair pins both halves of the contract; either alone is insufficient. (d) The CHECK / FK violation matrix for break_glass_sessions has FOUR distinct probes that surface as typed apierr.Conflict via mapWriteError: unknown organization (FK), blank actor_kind + unknown actor_kind (both fail the CHECK actor_kind IN ('usr','sa')), blank reason (CHECK length(reason) > 0), and expires_at <= started_at (CHECK expires_at > started_at — exercised with both equal-to-started_at AND predates-started_at sub-cases). The repository does NOT pre-validate these fields (the service buildSessionToCreate is the chokepoint for validation), so the constraint violation flows through the database CHECK and surfaces via mapWriteError. (e) The `twoOrgs(t, db, f, label)` helper is genuinely new at package scope (verified via grep on `^func twoOrgs` across all store_test files — no prior declaration exists) — it names the two-organization fixture pattern (a TARGET tenant + a SUPPORT actor's home tenant) that every break_glass test needs. The 28-test shape this file lands: Append-row-shape (raw-SQL byte-equal + bgs_ prefix + server-side timestamps within ±2s + version=1 + RevokedAt nil), Append-respects-caller-supplied-id, Append-duplicate-id-Conflict (PRIMARY KEY), Append-StartedAt-defaults-to-now (the load-bearing server-side-fill probe), four CHECK/FK-violation Conflicts (unknown-org, blank-actor_kind, unknown-actor_kind, blank-reason), expires_at-not-after-started_at-Conflict (equal + predate sub-cases), Append-nil-Tx-Internal, Append-transaction-rollback, Append-peer-row-byte-identical, Get-reads-back, Get-unknown-NotFound, Get-cross-tenant-NotFound, Get-expired-returns-row-as-is (Active(t) observation, NOT Get filtering), List-newest-first-ordering (started_at DESC, id DESC), List-limit-clamping matrix (non-positive / negative / above-cap / in-range), List-unknown-org-empty-slice, MarkRevoked-happy-path (RETURNING byte-equal raw-SQL + version+1 via bump_version + updated_at advance via set_updated_at), MarkRevoked-already-revoked-Conflict (does not move revoked_at/revoked_by_*), MarkRevoked-unknown-NotFound, MarkRevoked-cross-tenant-NotFound (does not touch row), MarkRevoked-nil-Tx-Internal, MarkRevoked-peer-row-byte-identical, append-mostly-trigger-rejects-column-rewrites (per-column matrix), append-mostly-trigger-rejects-blank-reason (trigger's leading guard), organization-DELETE-cascade. New helpers introduced (per-file BreakGlass-suffix to avoid store_test collisions): rawBreakGlassRow, loadBreakGlassRowByID, countBreakGlassRowsForOrg, mintBreakGlassSessionID, breakGlassSessionFixture, seedBreakGlassSession, assertBreakGlassRowByteIdentical, breakGlassTxRollbackSentinel, sanitizeTestNameForBreakGlassID, AND the package-new twoOrgs helper for the two-org fixture shape. REUSED verbatim from sibling files: assertTimePtrEqual (drift_finding_repository_invariants_test.go), seedOrg (schema_test.go), newStore (store_test.go), wantErrCode (idempotency_test.go). NO migration added (0019_break_glass_sessions l